// #465 ACCEPT arm for string_index_non_int_rejected.wyn. Making that rule fail
// the build could equally have been achieved by rejecting every string index, so
// a valid int subscript must still compile and return the single character.
// A variable subscript as well as a literal one: the rule is keyed on the index
// EXPRESSION's checked type, not on the literal node kind.
// EXPECT: e-l
s = "hello"
i = 3
print("${s[1]}-${s[i]}")
